<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Apolo Kagwa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1864–1927</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Sir Apolo Kagwa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Apolo Kagwa was katikkiro, or chief minister, of Buganda from 1889 to 1926. A leader of the Protestant party in the religious wars, he headed the regency for the infant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabaka-of-buganda">Kabaka</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daudi-chwa-ii">Daudi Chwa II</a> and negotiated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buganda-agreement">Buganda Agreement</a> of 1900 with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harry-johnston">Sir Harry Johnston</a>, which secured large estates for the chiefs. He also wrote histories of the kings and customs of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baganda">Baganda</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luganda">Luganda</a>.</p></div>
